target: internal/push/push.go
verify: go test ./internal/push/ -count=1 -run 'TestCheckDiagnosesBeingUnableToAsk'
expect: could not be run
why:    when NEITHER probe could run, the refusal still says "run pr-report.py --post first" — correct as a decision, because the gate fails closed, and the wrong instruction for a missing `gh`/`git` or a killed subprocess. The reason string cannot carry the difference: parity_test.go compares it byte-for-byte against push-check.py. So the one line that can say it goes to stderr, where neither implementation writes anything and nothing parses.
